* Single-switch DC probe (issue #92) -- ONE operating point, local.
* NOT a performance claim and NOT a record. This deck measures one number for
* one device at one corner: either the on-state resistance of a switch passing
* vcm = 0.9 V, or its off-state leakage with a drain-source bias across it.
* Simulated (ngspice, sky130 device models); nothing here is measured.
*
* It exists so the switch-resistance and leakage numbers quoted in
* design/integrator/SIZING.md ("Why the `vcm` switches need a PMOS half") have
* a committed testbench rather than resting on prose. The settling numbers
* those arguments lead to are a different bench (integrator-settling).
*
* run_probe.py substitutes the doubled-brace placeholders: PDK library and
* corner, temperature, supply, the device model and its geometry, the gate and
* bulk bias, and the two terminal voltages.
.lib {{PDK_LIB}} {{CORNER}}
.temp {{TEMP}}
Vdda vdda 0 {{VDDA}}
* Source sits at vcm; drain is offset by the probe bias. The current through
* Vd is the whole device current, so Ron = bias / I(Vd) in the on case and
* I(Vd) is the leakage in the off case.
Vs s 0 {{VS}}
Vd d 0 {{VD}}
Vg g 0 {{VG}}
Vb b 0 {{VB}}
X1 d g s b {{MODEL}} {{GEOM}}
.control
option gmin=1e-15
op
let i_dev = abs(i(vd))
let r_on = {{BIAS}}/i_dev
print i_dev r_on
.endc
.end
